The funny message occurs when you try to move. As a shrieker (or any
other F, I think) you get:
"Your rhizome gets stuck in a crevice."

Similar results are obtained with other types of creatures with
strange or non-existent limbs, such as sharks, gas spores, snakes,
etc.

There's a similar phenomenon involving worn rings. Unlike armor or
weapons, rings don't fall off when you polymorph into a creature that
can't equip them in the first place. Hence, it's possible to polymorph
into a snake and get an inventory listing that includes: "a ring of
slow digestion (on right scale gap)". The list of extremities for
rings is not the same as for stuck limbs.

Finally, you get yet another class of weird limb messages when
creatures walk into rust traps. My personal favorite is the v class,
which can produce: "A gush of water hits you on the central core!".
You can get different messages depending on where the water would have
hit you if you were humanoid. Ex., a shrieker can be hit "on the cap
area" as well as the "[left/right] mycelium"



